igious centre, and famous people linked to the town include Miguel Cervantes (baptized and almost certainly born here), author of Don Quixote, Cardinal Cisneros (refounder of the University of Alcalá, the current Complutense University of Madrid) and Katherine of Aragon (born here), first wife of England's King Henry VIII. Alcalá is easily visited as a day-trip from Madrid, and because it's so close to Madrid Barajas Airport it makes a good first or last night stop on a tour of northern Spain.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Alcalá de Henares","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Alcal%C3%A1_de_Henares","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Alcala de Henares, a UNESCO listed city in Spain, packs its old centre with colleges and churches. The Museo Casa Natal de Cervantes and the Archbishop's Palace lead, and the whole thing fills a day. April, May and September suit best.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":193751,"visit_h":7.4}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-cathedral-of-los-santos-ninos-justo-y-pastor-de-alcala-de-henares","name":"Cathedral of los Santos Niños Justo y Pastor de Alcalá de Henares","kind":"Cathedral","lat":40.48053,"lon":-3.36926,"dist_km":0.8,"rank_score":9.02,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Alcala_cathedral_2023_-_western_fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/960px-Alcala_cathedral_2023_-_western_fa%C3%A7ade.jpg","author":"Fernando","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcala_cathedral_2023_-_western_fa%C3%A7ade.jpg","w":5156,"h":6446,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-archbishop-s-palace-of-alcala-de-henares","name":"Archbishop's Palace of Alcalá de Henares","kind":"Palace","lat":40.48244,"lon":-3.36965,"dist_km":0.8,"rank_score":8.48,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Palacio_Arzobispal_de_Alcal%C3%A1_de_Henares_%28RPS_12-2-2012%2